// mayhem/errors_shim.go.src — a tiny stdlib-only stand-in for
// github.com/crossplane/crossplane-runtime/v2/pkg/errors, staged by
// mayhem/build.sh into the _mayhem_harness/dag mini-module at errors/errors.go.
//
// WHY: internal/dag/dag.go's ONLY non-stdlib import is crossplane-runtime's
// errors helper, and it uses just two symbols — errors.New and errors.Errorf.
// The real package pulls k8s.io/apimachinery + controller-runtime, which would
// drag crossplane's entire Kubernetes closure into the mini-module and defeat
// the point of isolating a dependency-light surface. These two shims are
// behaviorally identical for dag.go's use (New wraps a message, Errorf formats),
// so the fuzzed algorithm AND the oracle's "detected cycle on: X" message are
// exactly what upstream produces. The build.sh sed only repoints dag.go's import
// path at this shim; dag.go itself is copied verbatim.
package errors

import "fmt"

// New returns an error with the supplied message (stdlib errors.New semantics).
func New(message string) error { return fmt.Errorf("%s", message) }

// Errorf formats according to a format specifier and returns the error.
func Errorf(format string, args ...any) error { return fmt.Errorf(format, args...) }
